What is Software Testing?
Software testing is the process of evaluating an application or system to discover any gaps, errors, or missing requirements compared to the actual requirements. It includes functional testing (verifying that each feature works as intended) and non‑functional testing (assessing attributes such as speed, security, and usability). Modern testing spans manual exploratory techniques, scripted automation, and intelligent, AI‑augmented solutions that can generate test cases, self‑heal scripts, and predict high‑risk code paths.
