South American organisations adopt a pragmatic approach to quality assurance, prioritising cost‑sensitivity while gradually embracing automation. Brazil leads the conversation, with local service providers integrating testing services into broader digital‑enablement projects for banking and retail. The region’s growing regulatory awareness, especially around data‑privacy, nudges firms toward more systematic security testing practices. Despite economic headwinds, a steady stream of talent emerges from technical institutes, supporting a modest yet persistent shift toward cloud‑hosted testing environments.
Middle East & Africa
In the Middle East and Africa, government‑led digital agendas stimulate demand for robust testing frameworks, particularly in smart‑city and e‑government initiatives. The United Arab Emirates and Saudi Arabia champion the establishment of testing labs that align with emerging cybersecurity standards. African markets, while still developing core infrastructure, see testing activity concentrated around mobile‑money platforms and fintech startups, where rapid iteration necessitates lightweight yet reliable test suites. Partnerships with global cloud providers accelerate the diffusion of SaaS‑based testing tools, helping regional players meet rising expectations for reliability and security.
